# 1. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Transform LedgerAI PH into a centralized, enterprise-grade, on-premises ERP platform that supports multiple companies, multiple users, multiple client computers, and browser-based access through a central office server.

The intended architecture:

- One Windows PC acts as the central LedgerAI PH server.
- The server hosts the authoritative application backend, company registry, databases, documents, and storage.
- The server runs automatically in the background when Windows starts.
- Other computers and laptops connect through the same office LAN or Wi-Fi network.
- Users access LedgerAI PH using Chrome, Edge, Firefox, or other supported browsers.
- Users authenticate using their individual accounts.
- Users can select, open, and switch between authorized company profiles.
- Company databases remain centralized on the server.
- Client computers do not need to install or receive the complete LedgerAI PH application or company database files.

This must be implemented as an integrated architecture, not as a separate disconnected application.

Preserve existing LedgerAI PH accounting functionality, Philippine Tax Engine, Compliance Rule Engine, Document Management, OCR, AI capabilities, RBAC, audit trails, database lifecycle, and enterprise security.

Do not unnecessarily rewrite or replace existing working modules.

